{"additions":179,"assignees":[],"author":{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMTA5NDkz","is_bot":false,"login":"td72","name":"Kohei Hosokawa"},"body":"## Problem\n\nMoving down a list from the top and moving up from the bottom paged differently. Every list pane created a fresh `ListState` per frame, so ratatui recomputed the offset from nothing: any selection beyond the first page was pinned to the **bottom** row. Downwards that looks right (walk the page, then scroll one row at the edge); upwards the list scrolled immediately with the selection stuck on the last row until it re-entered the first page.\n\n## Fix\n\n- `theme::render_search_list` / `theme::render_list_pane` take the pane's kept scroll offset and return the new one (`ListState::with_offset` / `offset()`); the doc explains why.\n- Every list pane stores it in a `list_scroll` field: GitHub issue / PR / run lists, Git file tree / branches / reflog, Files, Docker containers / images, Worktrees / stashes, Projects list, the run Jobs tree.\n- The hand-rolled lists do the same: the Procs `render_table_pane` helper (processes, ports), the Files parent column, the Git log, and the PR **Checks** table (its `SubPaneScroll::scroll_y` doubles as the table offset; `render_status_table` now takes the `SubPaneScroll`).\n- The Projects board columns already kept their own offsets and were symmetric.\n\n## Test\n\n`kept_scroll_makes_list_scrolling_symmetric` (theme): renders through a `TestBackend` and asserts the offset stays put while the selection moves up within the page and moves one row at the top edge.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01TreGn5Xh4PjDRv9Yo4QU4w\n","changedFiles":19,"comments":[],"createdAt":"2026-09-10T10:25:17Z","deletions":32,"headRefName":"fix/list-scroll-symmetry","labels":[{"id":"LA_kwDORNPWJs8AAAACXrzvLA","name":"bug","description":"Something isn't working","color":"d73a4a"}],"number":192,"reviewDecision":"","reviewRequests":[],"reviews":[{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABM-m65g","author":{"login":"copilot-pull-request-reviewer"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"### 🟡 Changes recommended\n\nThe PR “Checks” table reuses `SubPaneScroll.scroll_y` as a table offset, which conflicts with existing navigation semantics and can make Up/Down behave incorrectly (plus there are empty/transient-state paths that reset kept offsets).\n\n*Once you've addressed the issues Copilot identified, you can request another Copilot review.*\n\n<details>\n<summary>Pull request overview</summary>\n\nThis PR fixes asymmetric list scrolling in the TUI by persisting ratatui scroll offsets across frames (instead of recreating `ListState`/`TableState` each render), so moving up and down through long lists behaves consistently throughout the app.\n\n**Changes:**\n- Updated `theme::render_search_list` / `theme::render_list_pane` (and the procs table helper) to accept a previous scroll offset and return the updated offset.\n- Added `list_scroll` state to most list/table panes and wired it into rendering so offsets persist across frames.\n- Added a `TestBackend`-based unit test asserting symmetric scrolling behavior.\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>File summaries</summary>\n\n| File | Description |\r\n| ---- | ----------- |\r\n| src/core/theme.rs | Changes list render helpers to take/return a kept scroll offset; adds a regression test for symmetric scrolling. |\r\n| src/worktrees/panes/worktrees.rs | Persists scroll offset for the Worktrees list pane via `list_scroll`. |\r\n| src/worktrees/panes/stashes.rs | Persists scroll offset for the Stashes list pane via `list_scroll`. |\r\n| src/projects/panes/projects.rs | Persists scroll offset for the Projects list pane via `list_scroll`. |\r\n| src/procs/panes/processes.rs | Persists scroll offset for the Processes table pane via `list_scroll` and updated helper signature. |\r\n| src/procs/panes/ports.rs | Persists scroll offset for the Ports table pane via `list_scroll` and updated helper signature. |\r\n| src/procs/panes/mod.rs | Updates `render_table_pane` to accept/return the scroll offset and reuse it via `ListState::with_offset`. |\r\n| src/github/panes/gh_list.rs | Persists scroll offset for GitHub list panes via `list_scroll`. |\r\n| src/github/panes/detail_view/view.rs | Updates PR “Checks” table rendering to keep a table offset (via `TableState::with_offset`) and returns it. |\r\n| src/github/panes/detail_view/jobs.rs | Persists scroll offset for the Actions Jobs tree list via `list_scroll` passed to `render_search_list`. |\r\n| src/git/panes/reflog.rs | Persists scroll offset for the Reflog list pane via `list_scroll`. |\r\n| src/git/panes/git_log/mod.rs | Adds `list_scroll` state to the Git Log pane. |\r\n| src/git/panes/git_log/view.rs | Uses `list_scroll` to keep the Git Log list offset across frames. |\r\n| src/git/panes/file_tree.rs | Persists scroll offset for the Git file tree pane via `list_scroll`. |\r\n| src/git/panes/branch_list.rs | Persists scroll offset for the Branches list pane via `list_scroll`. |\r\n| src/files/panes/parent_dir.rs | Persists scroll offset for the Files parent-dir column via `list_scroll`. |\r\n| src/files/panes/dir_list.rs | Persists scroll offset for the Files dir list pane via `list_scroll`. |\r\n| src/docker/panes/images.rs | Persists scroll offset for the Docker Images list pane via `list_scroll`. |\r\n| src/docker/panes/containers.rs | Persists scroll offset for the Docker Containers list pane via `list_scroll`. |\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>Review details</summary>\n\n### Suppressed comments (1)\n\n**src/github/panes/detail_view/view.rs:581**\n* `render_status_table` treats `SubPaneScroll.scroll_y` as the table’s offset, but `GhDetailViewPane::execute` uses `scroll_y` to decide whether MoveUp/MoveDown should scroll within an item vs move the selection. Once the table offset becomes non-zero, pressing Up will decrement `scroll_y` (offset) instead of moving `selected_idx`, which makes navigation behave incorrectly. This needs a separate persisted table-offset field (e.g. `status_table_scroll: usize`) or a `SubPaneScroll` redesign so selection navigation and offset don’t share the same variable.\n```\n) -> usize {\n    let (selected_idx, scroll) = (status.selected_idx, status.scroll_y as usize);\n    let block = sub_block(title, is_active, is_detail_focused);\n```\n\n- **Files reviewed:** 19/19 changed files\n- **Comments generated:** 3\n- **Review effort level:** Lite\n</details>\n\n---\n\n💡 <a href=\"/td72/vig/new/main?filename=.github/skills/code-review/SKILL.md\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Add a `code-review` agent skill</a> or configure MCP servers for context-aware, tailored reviews. <a href=\"https://docs.github.com/copilot/how-tos/use-copilot-agents/request-a-code-review/use-code-review?tool=webui#mcp-servers-and-agent-skills\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Learn more in the docs.</a>","submittedAt":"2026-09-10T10:28:42Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"6507ce4389ca4dc59048675354eb48f9f8b2c195"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABNHI2_g","author":{"login":"td72"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"","submittedAt":"2026-09-11T04:07:24Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"6507ce4389ca4dc59048675354eb48f9f8b2c195"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABNHI3og","author":{"login":"td72"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"","submittedAt":"2026-09-11T04:07:26Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"864959d85bd211c4ffe90542850a17eda26d814e"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABNHI4LA","author":{"login":"td72"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"","submittedAt":"2026-09-11T04:07:28Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"864959d85bd211c4ffe90542850a17eda26d814e"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABNHKSfA","author":{"login":"copilot-pull-request-reviewer"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"### 🟡 Changes recommended\n\nThe PR Checks table has unresolved scrolling behavior, and VHS demo artifacts need updating.\n\n*Once you've addressed the issues Copilot identified, you can request another Copilot review.*\n\n<details>\n<summary>Review details</summary>\n\n### Suppressed comments (1)\n\n**src/core/theme.rs:150**\n* This changes user-visible scrolling across every list pane, but the PR does not update the VHS demo tape/GIF artifacts that exercise these panes. Re-record the affected demos and include the tape/GIF changes so the new bidirectional scrolling behavior is covered by the project's visual integration artifacts.\n```\npub fn render_search_list(\n    f: &mut Frame,\n    area: Rect,\n    items: Vec<ListItem>,\n    block: Block,\n    selected_idx: Option<usize>,\n    match_set: &HashSet<usize>,\n    scroll: usize,\n) -> usize {\n```\n\n- **Files reviewed:** 19/19 changed files\n- **Comments generated:** 2\n- **Review effort level:** Lite\n</details>","submittedAt":"2026-09-11T04:12:04Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"864959d85bd211c4ffe90542850a17eda26d814e"}}],"state":"MERGED","statusCheckRollup":[{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-09-11T04:53:59Z","conclusion":"SKIPPED","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/34563918324/job/103152055846","name":"create-tag","startedAt":"2026-09-11T04:54:10Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Release"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-09-11T04:08:50Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/34561007736/job/103143541303","name":"build (x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu, ubuntu-latest)","startedAt":"2026-09-11T04:07:31Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Build"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-09-11T04:07:59Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/34561007762/